      "id": "clm_01M4VGNQYC9RC6097S0GK561MD",
      "statement": "The Ahasuerus and Artaxerxes of Ezra 4:6–23 are Xerxes I and Artaxerxes I, and the section concerns the rebuilding of the city walls in their reigns, placed here by topic.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Ezra.4.6-Ezra.4.23",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil (with Kleinert and Schultz) and Ryle identify the kings with Xerxes and Artaxerxes I: the names match, and the letter concerns the city and its walls, not the Temple. Ryle thinks the compiler inserted vv. 8–23 believing they concerned the Temple. Older expositors (reported by both) took the names as Cambyses and Pseudo-Smerdis to keep the narrative in order; Josephus addresses the letter to Cambyses; 1 Esdras keeps \"Artaxerxes\" but places the letter before Darius and adds the Temple's foundation.",
